/* ===== RELIGIOUS STUDIES · BENGALI (faith pack, July 2026) =====
   PRIMARILY FOR BENGALI PEOPLE (Kolkata / West Bengal) to learn about Jesus —
   Bengali is the primary language everywhere (titles, story text,
   explanations), with English the quiet second line. Mirrors faith/ne.js:
   the same two stories, the same 10+10 big-moment sections, the same shared
   scene art. Deliberately Christian (the secular-content rule does NOT apply
   in faith mode). Content register: rich storytelling for the un-churched
   reader — every person, place and church-word introduced in-story on first
   use (Adam & Eve, Eden, Noah, Abraham, sacrifice, the prophets, exile,
   disciples, Mary Magdalene). Paraphrase only — no Bible-translation text is
   copied; references name the passages retold.
   Vocabulary: ঈশ্বর (God), যীশু (Jesus), প্রভু (Lord), পাপ (sin), বিশ্বাস
   (faith), ভালোবাসা/প্রেম (love), পরিত্রাণ/উদ্ধার (salvation), ত্রাণকর্তা/
   উদ্ধারকর্তা (Rescuer), সুসমাচার (gospel), ক্রুশ (cross), পবিত্র আত্মা (Holy
   Spirit), প্রতিজ্ঞা (promise), নিয়ম (covenant), সহভাগিতা (fellowship),
   ভাববাদী (prophet), শিষ্য (disciple), বলিদান (sacrifice), নির্বাসন (exile).
   Register: honorific verb forms for God/Jesus (করলেন/বললেন/দিলেন, present
   করেন/আছেন, future করবেন) as in Bengali church usage. Romanization follows
   the Bengali course scheme in lang/bn.js (ASCII; inherent vowel & অ/ও = o;
   sh for শষস; dental+retroflex collapse to t/d in word roms). Native strings
   must avoid the chars \u0027 \u0022 < > \ (they ride inline onclick
   handlers — use dashes for speech, দাঁড়ি for sentence ends).
   IMPORTANT: keep paras[i][0] AND note[0] byte-stable once audio exists —
   clips in audio-bnf/ are hashed from these exact strings. Regenerate with
     osascript -l JavaScript extract_audio_strings.js bnf
     python3 generate_audio.py --lang bnf
   Scene art is shared with the Nepali pack (language-independent scene
   emblems — scenes and symbols only, no depictions of God or of Jesus'
   face). */

